* TMUX6136_BEH_v2.lib
* Behavioral model of one TMUX6136-style precision SPDT channel
* (not a TI model - built from datasheet parameters; verify values
*  against TMUX6136 datasheet tables 5.5/5.6 at +/-15 V)
*
* v2: convergence fixes
*   - logic threshold widened and smoothed
*   - charge injection driven from the slowed internal edge (X)
*     instead of the ideal step (X0): same total charge, spread
*     over ~TAU, so the op-amp input sees no ns-wide current spike
*   - ROFF/RON ratio reduced to 1e11
*
* Pin order: S1 S2 D SEL VDD VSS
* SEL low  -> S1 connected to D
* SEL high -> S2 connected to D
* Use two instances for the dual TMUX6136.
*
.SUBCKT SPDT_PREC S1 S2 D SEL VDD VSS
+ PARAMS: RON=120 CS=4p CD=6p QINJ=0.4p TAU=30n ILK=0.5p

* Logic threshold ~1.4 V (TTL-compatible), internal control 0..1 V
E_LOG  X0 0 TABLE {V(SEL)} = (1.0,0) (1.8,1)
R_T    X0 X  1k
C_T    X  0  {TAU/1k}

* Different switch thresholds -> automatic break-before-make
S_A  S1 NA  X 0 SW_A
S_B  S2 NB  X 0 SW_B
R_A  NA D  {RON}
R_B  NB D  {RON}
.MODEL SW_A VSWITCH (RON=0.1 ROFF=1e10 VON=0.3 VOFF=0.4)
.MODEL SW_B VSWITCH (RON=0.1 ROFF=1e10 VON=0.7 VOFF=0.6)

* Charge injection: smoothed 1 V internal edge through C = Q/1V
C_INJ  X  D  {QINJ/1}

* Parasitic capacitances and leakage
C_S1 S1 0 {CS}
C_S2 S2 0 {CS}
C_D  D  0 {CD}
I_LK D  0 DC {ILK}

* Supply pins not modeled; tie off so nodes are not floating
R_VDD VDD 0 1G
R_VSS VSS 0 1G
.ENDS SPDT_PREC
